Open the color picker when its swatch is tapped.

On a touch screen a tap on the swatch beside a CSS color only places the
caret. The picker opens from the editor's mouse down event (the default
editor.colorDecoratorsActivatedOn is clickAndHover), and a tap in the text
never raises one: the pointer handler ignores a touch pointer's down and moves
the caret from the tap gesture itself. A finger cannot hover either, so the
only picker left was the standalone one in the Command Palette, which changes
nothing in the file until its button is tapped.

Measured on an API 36 emulator (WebView 134): a real tap on the swatch gave
pointerdown, touchstart, pointerup, touchend and a tap gesture on
lines-content, no mousedown, and no picker. A mouse press at the same point
opened it.

Listen for the tap gesture and, when it began on a swatch, hand the swatch's
position to the code the mouse down runs. The setting still decides: "hover"
keeps a tap from opening anything. With the change the same tap opened the
picker, a tap and a drag inside it changed the color in the file as they went,
and a tap on other text closed it. The tap still places the caret, as the
click does.

